diff --git a/DOCS/man/options.rst b/DOCS/man/options.rst
index fa71dc0..d1b78cc 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -1181,6 +1181,29 @@ Video
     Specify the video output backend to be used. See `VIDEO OUTPUT DRIVERS`_ for
     details and descriptions of available drivers.
 
+``--decklink-mirror=<device>``
+    Additionally output the video, without OSD and subtitles, to a Blackmagic
+    DeckLink or UltraStudio device (Windows, requires Blackmagic Desktop
+    Video). ``auto`` uses the first device with an output, a number selects
+    a device by index, anything else selects the first device whose name
+    contains the string. Empty (default) disables it. ``dummy`` simulates a
+    device for testing (``dummy:<file>`` writes the output as raw UYVY).
+
+    The card runs on its own clock and shows each frame about 3 card frames
+    after the window does. Hardware decoded frames are copied back to system
+    memory. Cannot be changed at runtime.
+
+``--decklink-mode=<auto|mode>``
+    Output mode for ``--decklink-mirror``. ``auto`` (default) picks the mode
+    matching the video's frame rate and size, letterboxing video that does not
+    fill it. Otherwise one of the modes listed with ``-v``, e.g. ``1080p25``,
+    ``1080i50``, ``2160p25``, or a DeckLink mode code like ``Hp25``.
+
+``--decklink-delay=<seconds>``
+    Additional delay of the ``--decklink-mirror`` output (default: 0). Increase
+    it if frames are repeated or skipped on the output while they play
+    smoothly in the window.
+
 ``--vd=<...>``
     Specify a priority list of video decoders to be used, according to their
     family and name. See ``--ad`` for further details. Both of these options
